  "description": "The Sphinx II eBike is the evolution of our Sphinx. With a whole new frame and improved geometry, it features a longer reach, steeper seat tube, slacker head tube, and shorter chain stays to really tune its downhill capability.\nTo smooth out the trail there’s 130mm of bump absorbing travel at both ends, you’ll be flying down the black runs. Thanks to the high torque 110nm Ananda mid drive motor there’s no waiting for the uplift either, just pedal back up!\nWith a 15ah battery and clear LCD display, with built in USB charging port, you can keep rolling all day. More runs = More fun!\nTo keep you planted and gripped to those berms the Sphinx II has 34mm stanchion SR Suntour oil damped forks front and a DNM AO-38RC air sprung oil damped rear shock to keep things under control. Both have a lockout function to stiffen up the suspension when not needed. You can even ride to the trails!\nControl is everything at speed, and to make sure the Sphinx II handles as well as it looks we have installed 760mm bars, ergonomic grips, Shimano m200 hydraulic disc brakes, and 2.5” Maxxis Rekon tyres. It sticks as well as it shifts! Speaking of shifting…. The Sphinx II features MicroShift’s rugged Advent X 10 speed groupset with clutch mech ensure you never miss a gear. With a 34t no drop front chainring ring paired to a super wide 11-48t cassette you have all the range you need for the ups and downs. Take our word for it, the Sphinx II is colossal fun.\nPlease make sure to familiarise yourself with eBike and eScooter safety information before charging or using your new Reid. You can view and download user manuals and safety instructions here.",
